%N A402117 a(n) = Sum of the n-th row of a triangle whose n-th row consists of the n smallest available primes, where the k-th prime is removed after appearing in k rows.
%e A402117 Triangle of primes begins:
%e A402117   2,
%e A402117   3, 5,
%e A402117   3, 5, 7,
%e A402117   5, 7, 11, 13,
%e A402117   7, 11, 13, 17, 19,
%e A402117 The row sums are 2, 8, 15, 36, 67,...
%e A402117 Thus a(1) = 2, a(2) = 8, a(3) = 15, a(4) = 36, and a(5) = 67.
